{"name":"Sky High","hex":"#a7c2eb","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sky-high","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["extremely tall","excessive, exorbitant"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sky-high"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sky High (1922 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Sky High is a 1922 American silent Western film written and directed by Lynn Reynolds and starring Tom Mix, J. Farrell MacDonald, Eva Novak and Sid Jordan. The action in Sky High takes place in 1922 and while the characters ride horses and fight in saloons, they also use telephones, automobiles and even an aircraft."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/Skyhigh_poster.jpg/330px-Skyhigh_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sky_High_(1922_film)","wikidata":"Q1982924"},{"title":"Sky High (1951 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Sky High is a 1951 American comedy film directed by Sam Newfield and starring Sid Melton, Mara Lynn, Sam Flint, Douglas Evans and Fritz Feld. The film's music was composed by Bert Shefter."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/a/af/Sky_High_%281951_film%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sky_High_(1951_film)","wikidata":"Q39073538"},{"title":"Sky High (2005 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Sky High is a 2005 American superhero comedy film directed by Mike Mitchell and written by Paul Hernandez, and Kim Possible creators Bob Schooley and Mark McCorkle. Produced by Walt Disney Pictures, the film stars Kelly Preston, Michael Angarano, Danielle Panabaker, Mary Elizabeth Winstead and Kurt Russell. It follows Will Stronghold (Angarano), the son of two superheroes, who is enrolled in an airborne high school for teenage superheroes. As his dormant superpowers manifest, he struggles to maintain his relationships with his old friends, learns of a threat from a mysterious supervillain, and searches for the girl of his dreams."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/2/29/Sky_High_movie_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sky_High_(2005_film)","wikidata":"Q858508"},{"title":"Sky","blocks":[{"text":"The sky is an unobstructed view upward from the surface of the Earth. It includes the atmosphere and outer space. It may also be considered a place between the ground and outer space, thus distinct from outer space."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/July_night_sky_%2835972569256%29.jpg/330px-July_night_sky_%2835972569256%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sky","wikidata":"Q527"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/aa/Skyhigh1922-newspaperad.jpg/500px-Skyhigh1922-newspaperad.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/aa/Skyhigh1922-newspaperad.jpg/1280px-Skyhigh1922-newspaperad.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/aa/Skyhigh1922-newspaperad.jpg/500px-Skyhigh1922-newspaperad.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Newspaper advertisement","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASkyhigh1922-newspaperad.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/CSUN_Central_Campus.JPG/500px-CSUN_Central_Campus.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/CSUN_Central_Campus.JPG/1280px-CSUN_Central_Campus.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thu